tart":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"hAWa6UbeHR"}],"key":"wteJrsMHYq"}],"urlSource":"blog.md","dataUrl":"/blog.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"WLFvey1DJx"}],"key":"maQAH0pNt3"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recent blog posts","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"cqSl1Lcwbg"}],"identifier":"recent-blog-posts","label":"Recent blog posts","html_id":"recent-blog-posts","implicit":true,"key":"yH1OJ13Fcw"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A practical guide to beating jet lag","key":"ym2QEija1O"}],"key":"Y49SoiWVXZ"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"C5VXZgugWp"}],"key":"CGUPypbM5R"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"YUVb1zWOzZ"}],"key":"qWOWzBfWpN"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"tXNI0Cjyap"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"jtdyOQZuIh"}],"key":"o99cpGBk8R"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"eqChnDFAGG"}],"key":"apQHPH54LO"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","key":"hCD9w9hfGx"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"zGiEMLiA2X"}],"key":"nCDy9SmObL"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"L9V9qUihvc"}],"key":"OYcSkp2CXi"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"g79Wrcpi9s"}],"key":"J82v9ZrPbq"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"rWzmov9HrQ"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"dh729ckdly"}],"key":"Ta0p74CkQS"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"mWP0fd1QCV"}],"key":"DEBZDI5qgo"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","key":"r8VSwBwHI9"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"Mtome07xyn"}],"key":"Z7zrUqHfxz"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"vsOFkDYPlC"}],"key":"VlptwZlCwN"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"V5uRNcIAzQ"}],"key":"Sf3cDw5bR2"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"mfAQ5NZgqr"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"Ege4IpOvhW"}],"key":"ADSWLO8S8z"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"j66ehXSYKl"}],"key":"Kw1iQ2UR4r"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","key":"ZhZNpfQyIl"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"j0uOHv2Uvp"}],"key":"qcAyfo8lK4"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"lGL2YzLOzV"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"xWA6qawdRn"}],"key":"DO1RfoEB4b"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"F0ijzh8cJw"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"fMMCZYAPwN"}],"key":"SDIwLgPTlW"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"oDwv8GAZZr"}],"key":"EU2pxK8Af1"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"xYZ5JCiK0y"}],"key":"MGMyTCMhcw"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"FmhhZ71JN5"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"gSJFrV2v43"}],"key":"AUVhCdXZdQ"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"Bs4BVRuNbS"}],"key":"VQruzTAL4B"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","key":"nXHW0xJOBY"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"LCMboG1eWE"}],"key":"YIM07EhgiX"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"irbu9FiDKT"}],"key":"EQ2NQg7pB1"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"EmalqXWf94"}],"key":"eS5AYatk8N"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"ojfmUWsLEZ"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"kB8F9XLoJD"}],"key":"aQ0nyawk9Y"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"Y4orr1UyuJ"}],"key":"p85MwYoXCo"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","key":"mCWsctgaSe"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"NHg6lOaOWf"}],"key":"Xae5sdOV6N"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"YktedK7cse"}],"key":"iqcySi0zn0"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"yItFvL1HN4"}],"key":"kMdEMs7GQ5"},{"type":"text","value":"January 14, 2025 | ","key":"Qyeb6AKvHM"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"I4zNpAeFRs"}],"key":"K6kcFvNgrm"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"ZpgGQFFCah"}],"key":"BwbN5Lgrh7"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jec","key":"yMoisdvFO2"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/bluesky","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How I'm trying to use BlueSky without getting burned again","key":"vjAppy6H7S"}],"key":"tnH4mpOZBG"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some quick thoughts on moving from Twitter/X to BlueSky and how I'll try to use social media after being burned once by Twitter.\n","key":"IYFCMaK2UY"}],"key":"BlbGSKYyT1"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"zQr7u6HPFo"}],"key":"KE1M3GpK0C"},{"type":"text","value":"November 22, 2024 | ","key":"XnnvvtQkVG"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"FT0mykohha"}],"key":"ZWHvFvtskH"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"zydgSwh0u4"}],"key":"aKVAp095kc"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/bluesky","key":"sb5sMhXgtP"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/blog-list","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better blog lists with the MyST AST","key":"l2ial8XgdZ"}],"key":"rALP7b6HP7"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nOn my journey to learn more about writing with [the new MyST engine](https:///mystmd.org), I built upon [my recent update to my blog infrastructure](./programmatic-myst-with-jupyter.md) and made some improvements to my blog post list.\nHere's what it looks like now:\n\n````{note} Click here to see how it looks now\n:class: dropdown\n```{postlist}\n:number: 3\n```\n````\n\nHere's a quick rundown","key":"GAV5P7mzv7"}],"key":"r0T3mm2jMZ"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"mxJnwnhZTm"}],"key":"A5Jd6egltv"},{"type":"text","value":"November 09, 2024 | ","key":"C9mHY9Bldt"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"zNRUoId0L6"}],"key":"GvDwkHAOsT"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"m982QeZlTN"}],"key":"ZhVoUMBmZF"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/blog-list","key":"OPulbNQU5a"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate MyST with Jupyter and insert it into content programmatically","key":"mGUBJTp6ZR"}],"key":"non89h7Kic"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\n\nWhile I've been [converting my blog to use the new MyST engine](./mystmd-with-the-blog.md), I discovered a useful MyST feature. It's not yet possible to [natively parse Jupyter Markdown outputs as MyST](https://github.com/jupyter-book/mystmd/issues/1026) but there's a workaround if you don't mind generating a temporary file.\n\nThe trick is to _write to a temporary file_","key":"m2REupLNuy"}],"key":"bU2nO3C9dU"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"wbSZ5eDMXq"}],"key":"HICCw8VexR"},{"type":"text","value":"November 04, 2024 | ","key":"KonBd4RKFc"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"SC1chWE73R"}],"key":"XXnq5S272j"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"pfITdC4LiU"}],"key":"hQ0vRMMshb"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/programmatic-myst-with-jupyter","key":"J2bKiREaQi"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2024/mystmd-with-the-blog","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-building my blog with MySTMD","key":"eawFGp9hPA"}],"key":"fiREWZJxFF"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nWow it has been a long time since I've last-written here. It turns out that having two small children and a very demanding job means you don't have as much time for blogging. But that's a whole different blog post...\n\nI've decided to convert my blog to use the new [MyST","key":"XvmB9rLbRY"}],"key":"rpTChj2ZM7"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"usS6XQdvk9"}],"key":"aXpchca8xG"},{"type":"text","value":"November 01, 2024 | ","key":"h5CcekHYA9"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"y0akArHgfJ"}],"key":"R7Zi2MqtY5"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"mVWOFfOKRv"}],"key":"ENwwy8wprs"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2024/mystmd-with-the-blog","key":"V1X8Wd5IsK"}],"key":"y0M19AfufR"}],"key":"MsvcS5U3Cc"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"next":{"title":"About me","url":"/about","group":"Welcome"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}